{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]Beneath the [Dbdim6]cross of [Db]Jesus I [Ab7]fain would [Ebm7]take [Ab7]my[Db]stand,
[F7]The [Bbm]shadow of [F7]a[Bbm]might[Bb7]y[Ebm]rock [Bbm]with[Ebm7]in   a [Gb]weary [F]land;
[Db]A home within [Gb]the [Db]wil[Gb]der[Db7]ness, a [Gb]rest up[Bb]on the [Ebm]way,
From the [Ab7]burning of the [Db]noontide [Db]heat, [Gb]and the [Db]burden [Ab7]of the [Db]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db][Dbdim6]Upon [Db]that [Ab7][Ebm7]cross [Ab7]of [Db]Jesus
[F7][Bbm]mine [F7][Bbm]eye [Bb7]at [Ebm][Bbm]times [Ebm7][Gb]can [F]see
[Db][Gb]the [Db]very [Gb]dying [Db7][Gb]form [Bb]of [Ebm]One
[Ab7][Db]who [Db]suffered [Gb][Db]there [Ab7]for [Db]me;
[Db]and [Dbdim6]from [Db]my [Ab7]stricken [Ebm7]heart [Ab7]with [Db]tears
[F7][Bbm][F7]two [Bbm][Bb7]wonders [Ebm][Bbm][Ebm7]I [Gb][F]confess:
[Db][Gb]the [Db][Gb]wonders [Db7]of [Gb][Bb]redeeming [Ebm]love
[Ab7][Db][Db]and [Gb][Db]my [Ab7][Db]unworthiness.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db][Dbdim6]I [Db]take, [Ab7]O [Ebm7]cross, [Ab7]thy [Db]shadow
[F7][Bbm][F7]for [Bbm][Bb7]my [Ebm][Bbm][Ebm7]abiding [Gb][F]place;
[Db][Gb]I [Db]ask [Gb]no [Db7][Gb]other [Bb]sunshine [Ebm]than
[Ab7][Db]the [Db]sunshine [Gb][Db]of [Ab7]his [Db]face;
[Db]content [Dbdim6]to [Db]let [Ab7]the [Ebm7]world [Ab7]go [Db]by,
[F7][Bbm]to [F7][Bbm]know [Bb7]no [Ebm][Bbm]gain [Ebm7][Gb]nor [F]loss,
[Db][Gb]my [Db]sinful [Gb]self [Db7][Gb]my [Bb]only [Ebm]shame,
[Ab7][Db]my [Db]glory [Gb][Db]all [Ab7]the [Db]cross.
{end_of_verse}
